 is a single variable: counting, enumeration, direct access, and predicate elimination (i.e., transforming the pair of query and database to an equivalent pair without min-predicates). For each task, we establish a complete dichotomy for self-join-free CQs, precisely identifying the cases that are solvable in near-ideal time, i.e., (quasi)linear preprocessing time followed by constant or logarithmic time per output.
